1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,771
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,855 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:33,742
[Ivy] <i>Maybe this is exactly</i>
<i>what you deserve.</i>

6
00:00:33,825 --> 00:00:35,493
<i>Bye, Corruption Queen.</i>

7
00:00:35,577 --> 00:00:40,665
<i>You should take this opportunity</i>
<i>to assess your past actions.</i>

8
00:00:40,749 --> 00:00:43,293
<i>And you can do it all</i>
<i>in the comfort of this jail.</i>

9
00:00:43,376 --> 00:00:45,211
<i>Why are you punishing your own daughter?</i>

10
00:00:45,295 --> 00:00:48,256
<i>-Just shut up!</i>
<i>-You'll meet your maker one day.</i>

11
00:00:48,339 --> 00:00:52,135
<i>-Fifty million pesos.</i>
<i>-What do I get in return?</i>

12
00:00:52,218 --> 00:00:53,845
<i>I will become king,</i>

13
00:00:53,928 --> 00:00:57,515
<i>and you will be queen</i>
<i>of Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

14
00:00:57,599 --> 00:00:58,641
[Ivy] <i>Yes, Congressman.</i>

15
00:00:58,725 --> 00:01:02,645
<i>I'm with Sanggano right now,</i>
<i>and we're on our way</i>

16
00:01:02,729 --> 00:01:04,731
<i>to deliver the money</i>
<i>to the district chairmen.</i>

17
00:01:04,814 --> 00:01:07,400
<i>I'll do anything. Just get me out of here.</i>

18
00:01:07,484 --> 00:01:09,778
<i>I'll even turn my back</i>
<i>on my worthless father.</i>

19
00:01:09,861 --> 00:01:11,738
<i>If you aren't going to help Emilia,</i>

20
00:01:11,821 --> 00:01:14,032
<i>you might as well tell her the truth!</i>

21
00:01:14,115 --> 00:01:17,952
<i>That's right! Esmeralda wasn't</i>
<i>Emilia's mother.</i>

22
00:01:18,036 --> 00:01:21,748
<i>I took Emilia away to punish her,</i>

23
00:01:21,831 --> 00:01:27,253
<i>to make her feel the pain</i>
<i>that her mother put me through.</i>

24
00:01:27,337 --> 00:01:28,588
[Jose] <i>We're being followed.</i>

25
00:01:31,049 --> 00:01:32,175
<i>Don't you dare touch my money!</i>

26
00:01:32,258 --> 00:01:33,343
<i>-Hey!</i>
<i>-Mister Fernan!</i>

27
00:01:33,426 --> 00:01:38,056
<i>There's no way in hell you're</i>
<i>ever using my money, old man.</i>

28
00:01:38,139 --> 00:01:40,141
[Claire] <i>I will tell her the truth.</i>

29
00:01:40,225 --> 00:01:43,728
<i>So she can help Emilia break free</i>
<i>from a monster like you!</i>

30
00:01:43,812 --> 00:01:45,772
<i>Mrs. Emilia, Jaguar ordered us to get you.</i>

31
00:01:46,189 --> 00:01:49,609
[Julio] <i>Go after Clarita!</i>
<i>Shoot her if you have to!</i>

32
00:01:49,692 --> 00:01:51,861
<i>But do not let her leave this place alive!</i>

33
00:01:52,487 --> 00:01:56,616
<i>Esmeralda was not your real mother.</i>

34
00:01:56,699 --> 00:01:59,244
<i>Aunt Claire!</i>

35
00:01:59,327 --> 00:02:01,287
[Damian] <i>We have to take back</i>
<i>all the money</i>

36
00:02:01,371 --> 00:02:04,207
<i>Raul stole from me.</i>

37
00:02:08,128 --> 00:02:09,629
[gasps]

38
00:02:09,712 --> 00:02:10,588
<i>Dante?</i>

39
00:02:11,005 --> 00:02:12,048
<i>Dad?</i>

40
00:02:14,884 --> 00:02:17,554
[breathing heavily]

41
00:02:22,892 --> 00:02:23,935
Dad?

42
00:02:38,241 --> 00:02:39,284
[sobs]

43
00:02:39,701 --> 00:02:42,078
-[siren wailing]
-Auntie.

44
00:02:42,162 --> 00:02:43,955
Emilia, we need to leave right now.

45
00:02:44,038 --> 00:02:45,498
The cops will be here any minute.

46
00:02:45,582 --> 00:02:47,709
No, Jaguar. We cannot leave my aunt here.

47
00:02:47,792 --> 00:02:48,710
We can't!

48
00:02:48,793 --> 00:02:50,712
Aunt Claire!

49
00:02:50,962 --> 00:02:52,505
Aunt Claire!

50
00:02:52,589 --> 00:02:54,090
Emilia, we have to go!
It's dangerous out here.

51
00:02:54,173 --> 00:02:56,843
No! No!

52
00:02:57,427 --> 00:02:59,012
Jaguar, please!

53
00:02:59,470 --> 00:03:00,763
Listen to me, Emilia.

54
00:03:01,931 --> 00:03:03,975
I'm sorry for your loss,
but you aren't safe here.

55
00:03:04,058 --> 00:03:05,727
The police are looking for you.

56
00:03:07,896 --> 00:03:09,731
What about my aunt?

57
00:03:11,274 --> 00:03:14,110
Aunt Claire!

58
00:03:15,945 --> 00:03:18,531
Don't leave me!

59
00:03:20,742 --> 00:03:22,952
[wailing]

60
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:36,341
Dad?

61
00:03:36,925 --> 00:03:37,926
Dad?

62
00:03:42,305 --> 00:03:43,348
Lily…

63
00:03:45,391 --> 00:03:47,477
Lily, he's not your father.

64
00:03:49,771 --> 00:03:50,939
This isn't him.

65
00:03:52,649 --> 00:03:56,986
He's your Uncle Damian,
your dad's brother.

66
00:04:08,164 --> 00:04:12,460
Come on, dear. Let's take him home now.

67
00:04:15,630 --> 00:04:17,757
He's Dad's brother?

68
00:04:26,975 --> 00:04:29,811
[somber music playing]

69
00:04:40,029 --> 00:04:41,197
[sobs]

70
00:04:44,867 --> 00:04:46,995
Dad had a twin brother?

71
00:04:56,504 --> 00:04:59,132
[sobbing]

72
00:05:08,433 --> 00:05:11,019
[somber music playing]

73
00:05:27,952 --> 00:05:30,747
<i>You came all the way here</i>
<i>just to lecture me?</i>

74
00:05:30,830 --> 00:05:33,499
<i>-Please, leave me alone.</i>
<i>-I am just concerned, Emilia.</i>

75
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:34,709
<i>Papa!</i>

76
00:05:34,792 --> 00:05:37,920
<i>Why are you just standing there?</i>
<i>You have to do something.</i>

77
00:05:38,004 --> 00:05:39,547
-[Emilia] <i>No!</i>
-<i>There's nothing I can do.</i>

78
00:05:40,173 --> 00:05:42,717
<i>Auntie, don't tell me you're not</i>
<i>going to bail me out of here?</i>

79
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:45,011
<i>Why are you even here, then?</i>

80
00:05:45,094 --> 00:05:47,096
<i>I just want to be here for you.</i>

81
00:05:47,180 --> 00:05:49,766
<i>Auntie, it's not like I'm going to die.</i>

82
00:06:00,068 --> 00:06:01,903
[sobs]

83
00:06:07,450 --> 00:06:10,912
She was the only person who understood me.

84
00:06:12,580 --> 00:06:15,708
I would have gone completely mad
if it weren't for her.

85
00:06:17,919 --> 00:06:21,297
And now that she's gone,
I don't know what to do.

86
00:06:25,259 --> 00:06:29,055
Aunt Claire was one of the
kindest people I've ever known.

87
00:06:31,724 --> 00:06:33,559
I love her so much.

88
00:06:34,977 --> 00:06:37,605
I will always remember you.

89
00:06:39,941 --> 00:06:40,983
Emilia.

90
00:06:43,486 --> 00:06:44,654
That's enough.

91
00:06:46,906 --> 00:06:51,911
We need to leave now
before the cops track us here.

92
00:06:53,788 --> 00:06:57,583
I will order my men to take care
of things here for you.

93
00:06:59,293 --> 00:07:00,837
You know, Jaguar…

94
00:07:03,339 --> 00:07:05,883
my mom died when I was young.

95
00:07:09,011 --> 00:07:14,767
And she was one of the only few
who really loved me.

96
00:07:20,815 --> 00:07:23,317
She and the town were my whole life

97
00:07:23,401 --> 00:07:25,528
because Papa never loved me.

98
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:32,827
But apparently,
she wasn't even my real mother.

99
00:07:36,205 --> 00:07:39,041
My mom was the only one who loved me

100
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:41,544
the way Papa never did.

101
00:07:42,795 --> 00:07:45,965
That's why I need to find
my real mother, Jaguar.

102
00:07:49,093 --> 00:07:50,761
Please, help me.

103
00:07:59,353 --> 00:08:01,772
[sobbing]

104
00:08:15,161 --> 00:08:16,954
[crickets chirping]

105
00:08:27,924 --> 00:08:30,510
[soft instrumental playing]

106
00:08:40,728 --> 00:08:43,064
[soft instrumental playing]

107
00:08:52,782 --> 00:08:54,992
[soft instrumental playing]

108
00:09:13,719 --> 00:09:16,097
He looks exactly like Dad.

109
00:09:18,224 --> 00:09:23,604
I was really taken aback.

110
00:09:23,688 --> 00:09:25,690
It's almost as though
my father came back to life.

111
00:09:25,773 --> 00:09:27,692
[soft music playing]

112
00:09:29,235 --> 00:09:31,070
I do wonder, Mom…

113
00:09:34,865 --> 00:09:37,118
if Dad were still around…

114
00:09:41,163 --> 00:09:44,083
what kind of life would we have?

115
00:09:46,043 --> 00:09:47,336
Would it be a peaceful one?

116
00:09:48,921 --> 00:09:52,550
I mean, we'd be happy
because he'd be here.

117
00:09:54,302 --> 00:09:55,511
[sighs]

118
00:10:03,019 --> 00:10:05,229
After everything we went through…

119
00:10:10,484 --> 00:10:13,571
you'd probably think I'm strong.

120
00:10:16,115 --> 00:10:18,492
But to be honest, I get tired too.

121
00:10:23,331 --> 00:10:24,957
I can't be strong all the time.

122
00:10:33,674 --> 00:10:35,593
Come to think of it, if…

123
00:10:37,678 --> 00:10:39,639
If Dad were still alive,

124
00:10:40,514 --> 00:10:44,644
would he be pleased with what I'm doing?

125
00:10:48,606 --> 00:10:53,819
Sometimes, I wonder…

126
00:10:57,865 --> 00:11:02,953
Should I just continue what I started?

127
00:11:04,914 --> 00:11:07,833
Then again, the pain is still there.

128
00:11:10,378 --> 00:11:14,006
The pain they caused us is still there,

129
00:11:14,090 --> 00:11:15,633
and it still hurts.

130
00:11:19,970 --> 00:11:23,015
Sometimes, I wish we could just
leave everything behind…

131
00:11:25,518 --> 00:11:27,603
and move somewhere else…

132
00:11:28,813 --> 00:11:31,482
someplace where the two of us
can be happy.

133
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:38,989
I can only hope…

134
00:11:40,658 --> 00:11:43,619
that Dad understands what I'm doing, Mom.

135
00:11:48,290 --> 00:11:49,667
You're right, dear.

136
00:11:52,586 --> 00:11:55,714
If your father were still around,
our lives would be different.

137
00:11:57,758 --> 00:12:00,177
We wouldn't be going through all of this.

138
00:12:06,142 --> 00:12:12,898
But that doesn't mean he'd be
against what we've been doing.

139
00:12:13,441 --> 00:12:15,359
If he were still alive,

140
00:12:16,652 --> 00:12:18,946
I'm sure that he'd be fighting
by our side.

141
00:12:22,408 --> 00:12:24,702
Because there's no greater life

142
00:12:24,785 --> 00:12:29,373
than one devoted to fighting
for the greater good.

143
00:12:32,543 --> 00:12:38,174
A life where you put the good of others
above your own interests.

144
00:12:39,508 --> 00:12:43,888
That's probably what
your father would say.

145
00:12:47,057 --> 00:12:49,643
And if he were still around, dear…

146
00:12:51,770 --> 00:12:53,272
I'm sure he'd be so proud of you.

147
00:13:03,866 --> 00:13:04,992
[sighs]

148
00:13:15,794 --> 00:13:17,254
Thank you, Jaguar.

149
00:13:18,172 --> 00:13:22,218
Emilia, I'm here with you now.

150
00:13:24,094 --> 00:13:25,513
You will never be alone again.

151
00:13:26,680 --> 00:13:30,309
I know. But first things first.

152
00:13:30,976 --> 00:13:33,479
I have to find out who killed Aunt Claire.

153
00:13:38,943 --> 00:13:39,944
All right.

154
00:13:48,619 --> 00:13:50,704
Did you burn the body?

155
00:13:55,376 --> 00:13:56,502
Did you bury it?

156
00:14:01,173 --> 00:14:02,883
Did you throw it in the river?

157
00:14:08,264 --> 00:14:09,557
Or feed it to the dogs?

158
00:14:17,773 --> 00:14:19,942
None of the above?

159
00:14:20,776 --> 00:14:24,613
Then where the heck is Clarita's body?!

160
00:14:27,366 --> 00:14:30,077
Well, listen up, morons.

161
00:14:31,287 --> 00:14:33,789
Get out of here, and find her body.

162
00:14:33,873 --> 00:14:36,876
You're not coming back here until you find

163
00:14:36,959 --> 00:14:39,461
Clarita's rotting corpse.

164
00:14:39,753 --> 00:14:42,423
I don't care if you have
to search every nook

165
00:14:42,506 --> 00:14:45,009
and cranny of Poblacion Ardiente.

166
00:14:46,385 --> 00:14:47,428
Go!

167
00:14:52,266 --> 00:14:53,517
As for you, Colonel…

168
00:14:54,643 --> 00:14:58,230
Have you handed the money to Miss Aguas?

169
00:14:58,314 --> 00:15:00,232
I'm talking about the money
to be distributed

170
00:15:00,316 --> 00:15:02,318
to the district chairmen
to buy the people's votes.

171
00:15:03,652 --> 00:15:08,198
Congressman, Diego Torillo ambushed us.

172
00:15:08,657 --> 00:15:11,535
He could surrender the money to the police

173
00:15:11,619 --> 00:15:13,412
and find out about our operation.

174
00:15:15,164 --> 00:15:18,083
You insolent piece of trash!

175
00:15:19,376 --> 00:15:23,631
I gave you a simple job to do,
and you bungled it!

176
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:27,801
Get out of my sight!

177
00:15:33,515 --> 00:15:36,977
Why am I surrounded by brainless people?!

178
00:15:40,814 --> 00:15:42,441
I don't deserve this.

179
00:15:45,986 --> 00:15:48,614
Why is Uncle Damian here?

180
00:15:49,698 --> 00:15:52,576
And how did he get shot?

181
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:57,331
I hope I'm wrong.
But as far as I remember,

182
00:15:57,414 --> 00:15:59,583
Damian caused nothing
but trouble for your father.

183
00:16:03,379 --> 00:16:06,590
<i>Our daughter is so pretty.</i>
<i>What would you like to name her?</i>

184
00:16:06,674 --> 00:16:10,803
<i>-I was hoping to name her Lily.</i>
<i>-Lily?</i>

185
00:16:10,886 --> 00:16:13,472
<i>Yes. Isn't that nice?</i>

186
00:16:16,976 --> 00:16:18,018
<i>Damian.</i>

187
00:16:18,686 --> 00:16:22,189
<i>Why are you here so early?</i>
<i>Did you skip class again?</i>

188
00:16:24,775 --> 00:16:25,818
<i>Dante.</i>

189
00:16:27,444 --> 00:16:31,281
<i>Damian, look at your niece.</i>
<i>We named her Lily.</i>

190
00:16:35,035 --> 00:16:36,829
<i>What about you, Damian?</i>

191
00:16:36,912 --> 00:16:39,832
<i>Don't you want to have your</i>
<i>own family like your brother?</i>

192
00:16:42,001 --> 00:16:46,755
<i>I don't need a family.</i>
<i>What I need is to get rich.</i>

193
00:16:47,381 --> 00:16:49,216
<i>That way, I can finally do you both proud.</i>

194
00:16:49,299 --> 00:16:50,884
<i>How will you do that?</i>

195
00:16:50,968 --> 00:16:53,095
<i>You're not even focused on your studies.</i>

196
00:16:53,178 --> 00:16:58,600
<i>Why? Is school the only way</i>
<i>to succeed in life?</i>

197
00:16:58,684 --> 00:17:00,185
<i>And cutting classes…</i>

198
00:17:01,311 --> 00:17:03,772
<i>and living like a crook</i>
<i>will help you succeed in life?</i>

199
00:17:03,856 --> 00:17:05,190
[Camia] <i>Dante, that's enough.</i>

200
00:17:11,113 --> 00:17:12,281
[door closes]

201
00:17:20,205 --> 00:17:24,877
Lily, your father did everything he could

202
00:17:24,960 --> 00:17:27,129
to get Damian on the right track.

203
00:17:28,464 --> 00:17:30,132
But he chose to leave his family.

204
00:17:33,260 --> 00:17:35,596
I just hope he's changed.

205
00:17:49,234 --> 00:17:50,861
[crickets chirping]

206
00:17:51,904 --> 00:17:52,946
Jepoy.

207
00:17:53,572 --> 00:17:56,200
Jepoy, wait. Are you even listening to me?

208
00:17:56,283 --> 00:17:57,743
-Anna…
-Where are you going?

209
00:17:57,826 --> 00:17:59,620
Anna, please. I have to go.

210
00:17:59,703 --> 00:18:01,497
But where are you going?

211
00:18:01,872 --> 00:18:05,084
You've been gone for days,
and now you're leaving again?

212
00:18:05,459 --> 00:18:07,669
I'm sorry, Anna. I just really need to go.

213
00:18:07,753 --> 00:18:11,298
No, Jepoy. Just stay here
until Lily comes back.

214
00:18:11,381 --> 00:18:13,759
Otherwise, I'd find out
where you're always off to

215
00:18:13,842 --> 00:18:15,844
and whom you've been meeting up with.

216
00:18:16,637 --> 00:18:19,848
[tense music playing]

217
00:18:24,353 --> 00:18:25,896
[birds chirping]

218
00:18:35,906 --> 00:18:38,534
Why do I have this sinking feeling…

219
00:18:39,451 --> 00:18:42,079
that these incidents are connected?

220
00:18:43,497 --> 00:18:44,581
[sighs]

221
00:18:44,957 --> 00:18:45,958
Colonel.

222
00:18:48,418 --> 00:18:49,461
Yes, Congressman?

223
00:18:50,671 --> 00:18:55,509
I want you to investigate
how Emilia escaped from prison.

224
00:18:56,385 --> 00:18:58,846
And don't show your face here
until you find out.

225
00:18:59,388 --> 00:19:01,431
-Yes, Congressman.
-Okay.

226
00:19:02,975 --> 00:19:04,560
[phone ringing]

227
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:10,190
Hello?

228
00:19:18,782 --> 00:19:21,368
[tense music playing]

229
00:19:31,086 --> 00:19:33,672
[soft instrumental playing]

230
00:19:44,850 --> 00:19:46,935
[soft instrumental playing]

231
00:20:01,491 --> 00:20:06,580
[soft instrumental playing]

232
00:20:13,128 --> 00:20:14,129
Dad.

233
00:20:15,172 --> 00:20:16,506
[groans]

234
00:20:25,265 --> 00:20:26,266
[grunts]

235
00:20:26,725 --> 00:20:28,936
Who are you? Why am I here?

236
00:20:33,190 --> 00:20:34,233
Damian.

237
00:20:36,276 --> 00:20:38,946
[tense music playing]

238
00:20:48,372 --> 00:20:50,832
[tense music playing]

239
00:21:00,717 --> 00:21:01,760
Emilia?

240
00:21:03,220 --> 00:21:04,972
I'm glad you came, Papa.

241
00:21:05,389 --> 00:21:07,641
We can finally lay Aunt Claire to rest.

242
00:21:10,978 --> 00:21:13,397
[ominous music playing]

243
00:21:21,071 --> 00:21:21,947
Surprised?

244
00:21:23,115 --> 00:21:24,116
Not really.

245
00:21:24,950 --> 00:21:29,079
I'm actually more surprised…

246
00:21:29,997 --> 00:21:35,711
that it took you this long
to get out of jail.

247
00:21:35,794 --> 00:21:37,170
Why didn't you help me?

248
00:21:38,964 --> 00:21:40,966
-Emilia…
-Come on, Papa!

249
00:21:41,591 --> 00:21:43,677
Why did you let me go to jail?

250
00:21:44,177 --> 00:21:47,556
You even went after Aunt Claire too.

251
00:21:48,682 --> 00:21:50,309
Preposterous.

252
00:21:50,392 --> 00:21:51,852
There's no use denying it, Papa,

253
00:21:51,935 --> 00:21:54,271
because your men are a bunch of failures!

254
00:21:55,147 --> 00:21:56,732
Why did you have Aunt Claire killed?

255
00:21:57,482 --> 00:22:00,193
Did you kill her to cover up some secret?

256
00:22:01,862 --> 00:22:03,363
Now, you wait a minute.

257
00:22:04,906 --> 00:22:05,991
Hold on!

258
00:22:06,074 --> 00:22:08,869
Why am I suddenly on the hot seat?

259
00:22:09,369 --> 00:22:14,374
The thing is, you've got a lot
of questions to answer too.

260
00:22:14,458 --> 00:22:18,503
Let's play a game, shall we? It's called,

261
00:22:18,587 --> 00:22:23,550
"You Tell Me Your Secrets,
And I'll Tell You Mine."

262
00:22:25,302 --> 00:22:26,344
Let's start.

263
00:22:27,804 --> 00:22:30,557
How, in heaven's name…

264
00:22:32,350 --> 00:22:38,023
did my beautiful daughter,
a fugitive at that,

265
00:22:39,357 --> 00:22:41,943
get out of jail?

266
00:22:45,572 --> 00:22:46,573
Hmm?

267
00:22:47,949 --> 00:22:51,661
[ominous music swelling]

268
00:22:53,830 --> 00:22:56,708
Or should we just set aside

269
00:22:56,792 --> 00:23:00,003
the question-and-answer portion
for much later?

270
00:23:02,172 --> 00:23:05,092
Why don't we have… dinner at home?

271
00:23:06,593 --> 00:23:09,930
It would be a more relaxing setting.

272
00:23:10,680 --> 00:23:13,934
I'm sure you missed the mansion.

273
00:23:17,938 --> 00:23:19,773
I'm glad you asked, Papa.

274
00:23:20,273 --> 00:23:23,193
But first, I have to go somewhere.

275
00:23:24,111 --> 00:23:29,616
Okay. Then let's leave
this morbid location.

276
00:23:37,165 --> 00:23:38,375
Camia?

277
00:23:38,875 --> 00:23:39,793
Damian.

278
00:23:41,002 --> 00:23:42,671
I saw you on the street.

279
00:23:42,754 --> 00:23:46,133
You were bleeding, so I helped you.

280
00:23:46,925 --> 00:23:48,051
What are you doing here?

281
00:23:49,427 --> 00:23:53,515
When Dante died, I thought you'd
never come back to this place.

282
00:23:56,726 --> 00:23:58,019
It's a long story.

283
00:24:01,731 --> 00:24:07,195
But, Damian, why didn't you
visit us when your brother died?

284
00:24:10,031 --> 00:24:13,869
<i>Dante! I need your help.</i>
<i>Get me out of here.</i>

285
00:24:13,952 --> 00:24:17,581
<i>I've told you so many times,</i>
<i>but you still haven't changed.</i>

286
00:24:17,664 --> 00:24:19,875
<i>We may be brothers, but I won't think</i>
<i>twice about having you locked up</i>

287
00:24:19,958 --> 00:24:21,334
<i>if that's what it takes</i>
<i>to set you straight.</i>

288
00:24:21,418 --> 00:24:24,045
<i>Some brother you turned out to be!</i>

289
00:24:24,129 --> 00:24:26,298
[laughs mockingly]

290
00:24:26,882 --> 00:24:29,676
<i>That's how Jaguar works.</i>

291
00:24:29,759 --> 00:24:34,764
<i>If you're smart and sharp,</i>
<i>it'll rain cash!</i>

292
00:24:38,435 --> 00:24:41,146
PUBLIC ATTORNEY FOUND DEAD
IN POBLACION ARDIENTE

293
00:24:48,570 --> 00:24:50,739
<i>Are we still going to Poblacion Ardiente?</i>

294
00:24:51,489 --> 00:24:53,366
<i>No. Let's go back.</i>

295
00:24:58,496 --> 00:24:59,623
I didn't go to his funeral

296
00:24:59,706 --> 00:25:02,375
because he never cared for me, right?

297
00:25:02,459 --> 00:25:05,670
Damian, that's not true. Dante loved you.

298
00:25:05,754 --> 00:25:09,883
He did everything he could
to get you out of prison.

299
00:25:09,966 --> 00:25:11,092
He worked on your case.

300
00:25:11,176 --> 00:25:13,303
He came back for you,
but you were gone by then.

301
00:25:14,638 --> 00:25:17,766
<i>Dante, take it easy.</i>
<i>You'll ruin the surprise.</i>

302
00:25:17,849 --> 00:25:19,809
<i>I can't wait to tell him</i>
<i>about the schedule of the trial.</i>

303
00:25:19,893 --> 00:25:21,811
<i>This is his chance at freedom.</i>

304
00:25:21,895 --> 00:25:23,563
<i>I know he will change for the better.</i>

305
00:25:24,147 --> 00:25:28,485
<i>Sir, can I please talk to Damian Cruz?</i>

306
00:25:28,568 --> 00:25:30,612
<i>Oh, he's gone. He escaped.</i>

307
00:25:34,866 --> 00:25:37,953
Believe me, your brother loved
you very much.

308
00:25:38,036 --> 00:25:41,706
All he ever wanted
was for you to be happy.

309
00:25:46,044 --> 00:25:48,505
[soft instrumental playing]

310
00:25:58,473 --> 00:25:59,516
Damian.

311
00:26:04,980 --> 00:26:06,898
I know how you feel.

312
00:26:08,775 --> 00:26:09,818
[exhales]

313
00:26:09,901 --> 00:26:12,404
I felt the same thing
when your brother died.

314
00:26:14,990 --> 00:26:19,536
If you only knew how much
we suffered when he was gone.

315
00:26:36,636 --> 00:26:37,637
Lily.

316
00:26:39,973 --> 00:26:40,974
Damian.

317
00:26:43,810 --> 00:26:48,189
This is Lily, my daughter.

318
00:26:48,481 --> 00:26:49,816
She's your niece.

319
00:26:50,734 --> 00:26:51,735
Lily?

320
00:26:55,280 --> 00:26:56,448
It's okay, Lily.

321
00:26:59,868 --> 00:27:01,411
Have a seat, Lily.

322
00:27:05,707 --> 00:27:06,791
You've grown so much.

323
00:27:09,377 --> 00:27:13,131
Damian, I need to ask you a favor.

324
00:27:14,341 --> 00:27:18,928
Can you please not tell anyone
that you saw me and Lily?

325
00:27:22,807 --> 00:27:23,808
Why not?

326
00:27:24,726 --> 00:27:28,772
It's a long story,
but you'll find out soon enough.

327
00:27:36,988 --> 00:27:38,031
Lily.

328
00:27:41,451 --> 00:27:42,452
Um…

329
00:27:44,537 --> 00:27:51,044
Uncle Damian, if you don't mind me asking…

330
00:27:52,754 --> 00:27:55,757
what are you doing here
at Poblacion Ardiente?

331
00:27:56,966 --> 00:27:58,968
And how did you get shot?

332
00:27:59,052 --> 00:28:00,595
[tense music playing]

333
00:28:01,137 --> 00:28:02,097
[gunshot]

334
00:28:05,183 --> 00:28:07,727
[panting]

335
00:28:14,150 --> 00:28:16,945
I was ambushed by an armed man.

336
00:28:18,238 --> 00:28:19,280
He robbed me.

337
00:28:22,784 --> 00:28:24,911
I didn't think armed goons

338
00:28:24,994 --> 00:28:27,705
have become rampant here
in Poblacion Ardiente.

339
00:28:29,541 --> 00:28:30,625
[groans]

340
00:28:43,388 --> 00:28:45,807
You know, Uncle Damian, since…

341
00:28:47,642 --> 00:28:50,395
you're new around here…

342
00:28:52,689 --> 00:28:54,399
you should always be on guard.

343
00:28:55,775 --> 00:28:58,945
This town is full of two-faced bastards.

344
00:28:59,738 --> 00:29:01,865
They're very good
at putting up a good front,

345
00:29:01,948 --> 00:29:04,951
but they will show their true
intentions soon enough.

346
00:29:05,952 --> 00:29:09,080
They're the ones capable
of committing crimes.

347
00:29:26,264 --> 00:29:29,893
Diego, this will be
your temporary headquarters.

348
00:29:29,976 --> 00:29:32,270
You can't go back home yet.

349
00:29:36,065 --> 00:29:37,817
Your money's safe and sound now.

350
00:29:37,901 --> 00:29:40,904
Good thing Julio
didn't get his hands on it.

351
00:29:42,947 --> 00:29:45,200
The money isn't important, Diego.

352
00:29:45,283 --> 00:29:47,702
What matters is you're safe.
You're all safe.

353
00:29:47,952 --> 00:29:50,997
[soft music playing]

354
00:30:05,637 --> 00:30:06,763
Jepoy!

355
00:30:13,520 --> 00:30:15,939
I'm glad you got away from Jaguar.

356
00:30:16,773 --> 00:30:17,690
I needed to.

357
00:30:22,654 --> 00:30:23,988
[phone ringing]

358
00:30:26,491 --> 00:30:27,534
Excuse me.

359
00:30:28,993 --> 00:30:30,370
Yes, Congressman?

360
00:30:31,037 --> 00:30:32,372
Miss Aguas.

361
00:30:33,790 --> 00:30:36,209
I heard what happened. Are you okay?

362
00:30:39,587 --> 00:30:43,967
Well, Congressman, I'm trying
my best to cope with things.

363
00:30:44,217 --> 00:30:47,971
Oh. Poor girl.

364
00:30:49,430 --> 00:30:50,640
Why don't you come over?

365
00:30:50,723 --> 00:30:53,810
I can help you recover and

366
00:30:54,477 --> 00:30:56,604
<i>you can see Emilia if you want.</i>

367
00:30:59,941 --> 00:31:00,984
Emilia?

368
00:31:02,277 --> 00:31:05,280
Wait, Congressman, I thought
you had no plans

369
00:31:05,363 --> 00:31:06,865
of bailing Emilia out.

370
00:31:06,948 --> 00:31:08,199
[chuckles]

371
00:31:08,283 --> 00:31:09,492
It's a long story.

372
00:31:10,285 --> 00:31:14,414
Anyway, please do come. At about seven.

373
00:31:14,873 --> 00:31:18,543
So we can have a small
get-together of sorts.

374
00:31:23,756 --> 00:31:25,592
Excuse me. I need to go.

375
00:31:25,925 --> 00:31:28,136
Diego, Anna, Jepoy.

376
00:31:33,308 --> 00:31:35,977
[tense music playing]

377
00:31:44,569 --> 00:31:50,533
Colonel, are you sure
Miss Aguas is responsible

378
00:31:50,617 --> 00:31:51,951
for this screw-up?

379
00:31:53,161 --> 00:31:54,746
Yes, I'm sure, Congressman.

380
00:31:55,663 --> 00:31:56,706
Hmm.

381
00:31:58,082 --> 00:32:00,710
In that case, we'll make her pay for it.

382
00:32:01,669 --> 00:32:07,258
Oh, and please make sure
you find out where Emilia is.

383
00:32:08,384 --> 00:32:10,011
I'm not done with her yet.

384
00:32:13,473 --> 00:32:15,224
Seriously, these people…

385
00:32:19,771 --> 00:32:22,273
Damian. You're finally awake.

386
00:32:22,357 --> 00:32:24,317
Hold on, I'll make some breakfast.

387
00:32:29,155 --> 00:32:31,491
[soft instrumental playing]

388
00:32:37,789 --> 00:32:42,502
<i>Whatever feelings you had,</i>
<i>that's all in the past.</i>

389
00:32:43,378 --> 00:32:46,506
<i>You're not supposed to have feelings</i>

390
00:32:46,589 --> 00:32:48,174
<i>for her anymore, Damian.</i>

391
00:33:01,020 --> 00:33:03,189
<i>-It's her! It's her.</i>
<i>-Now's your chance.</i>

392
00:33:03,690 --> 00:33:05,608
<i>-Hold this.</i>
<i>-I'm sure you'll back out again.</i>

393
00:33:05,692 --> 00:33:07,068
<i>Me, back out? Shut up. I won't.</i>

394
00:33:07,860 --> 00:33:09,404
<i>Hey! My bag!</i>

395
00:33:10,780 --> 00:33:13,616
<i>-Hey!</i>
<i>-Call the cops!</i>

396
00:33:13,700 --> 00:33:18,204
<i>Sir! Sir, that's enough!</i>
<i>Thank you. That's enough.</i>

397
00:33:18,287 --> 00:33:20,915
<i>Let the police take care of him.</i>

398
00:33:22,959 --> 00:33:24,127
<i>The police?</i>

399
00:33:24,210 --> 00:33:27,964
<i>They'll just let him walk free</i>
<i>if he posts bail.</i>

400
00:33:28,548 --> 00:33:29,424
<i>Got it?</i>

401
00:33:29,507 --> 00:33:31,759
<i>People like him deserve</i>
<i>to have their hands chopped off!</i>

402
00:33:34,595 --> 00:33:35,680
<i>Anyway, here's your bag.</i>

403
00:33:36,931 --> 00:33:39,559
<i>-It's good as new, miss.</i>
<i>-Thank you.</i>

404
00:33:39,851 --> 00:33:41,019
<i>I'm Damian, by the way.</i>

405
00:33:45,732 --> 00:33:48,818
<i>-What's your name?</i>
<i>-Uh…</i>

406
00:33:50,028 --> 00:33:50,903
-<i>Well?</i>
-[Camia grunts]

407
00:33:51,696 --> 00:33:52,947
-[Camia groans]
-[Damian] Oh.

408
00:33:56,868 --> 00:33:58,578
<i>-Camia.</i>
<i>-Camia?</i>

409
00:33:58,870 --> 00:34:01,456
<i>You know, Camia, it's dangerous</i>
<i>around these parts.</i>

410
00:34:02,665 --> 00:34:04,292
<i>Maybe I should walk you home.</i>

411
00:34:04,375 --> 00:34:07,128
<i>-No, thank you. I can manage.</i>
<i>-Are you okay?</i>

412
00:34:07,211 --> 00:34:09,130
<i>-Thank you.</i>
<i>-Are you sure?</i>

413
00:34:09,213 --> 00:34:10,840
<i>-I hope you didn't get hurt.</i>
<i>-No.</i>

414
00:34:10,923 --> 00:34:12,925
<i>-Can you walk?</i>
<i>-I'm fine, thank you.</i>

415
00:34:15,219 --> 00:34:16,554
<i>What a beautiful name.</i>

416
00:34:17,972 --> 00:34:19,140
<i>-Camia…</i>
<i>-Thank you.</i>

417
00:34:19,223 --> 00:34:22,810
<i>Miss, are you all right?</i>
<i>I saw this man steal your bag.</i>

418
00:34:29,150 --> 00:34:30,068
<i>You're twins?</i>

419
00:34:30,902 --> 00:34:32,904
<i>No, we just look alike.</i>

420
00:34:34,572 --> 00:34:36,699
<i>This is my older brother, Dante.</i>

421
00:34:37,909 --> 00:34:40,578
<i>Dante, this is my friend, Camia.</i>

422
00:34:40,995 --> 00:34:41,996
<i>Hi.</i>

423
00:34:54,008 --> 00:34:55,927
<i>Do you want to report</i>
<i>the incident to the police?</i>

424
00:35:06,145 --> 00:35:07,688
[Dante] <i>Just eat up.</i>

425
00:35:08,606 --> 00:35:10,066
<i>I'm glad you came.</i>

426
00:35:11,275 --> 00:35:13,861
<i>You skipped school again</i>
<i>because of your side gig.</i>

427
00:35:14,320 --> 00:35:16,239
<i>You know that's illegal, right?</i>

428
00:35:17,240 --> 00:35:19,283
<i>Dante, stop lecturing me already.</i>

429
00:35:20,284 --> 00:35:22,912
<i>Let's just talk about</i>
<i>why you called me here.</i>

430
00:35:23,663 --> 00:35:24,622
<i>What's this about?</i>

431
00:35:25,665 --> 00:35:28,626
<i>It's about… Camia.</i>

432
00:35:31,170 --> 00:35:32,463
<i>I want to court her.</i>

433
00:35:32,547 --> 00:35:35,174
[fork thumps]

434
00:35:36,759 --> 00:35:38,845
<i>That's all right with you, isn't it?</i>

435
00:35:46,102 --> 00:35:47,311
[Damian groans]

436
00:35:51,774 --> 00:35:56,362
Damian, are you sure you don't
want to go to the hospital?

437
00:35:56,445 --> 00:35:57,738
Uh…

438
00:35:58,239 --> 00:36:00,366
No need. I'm fine.

439
00:36:01,242 --> 00:36:03,494
Or are you just refusing
to go to the hospital

440
00:36:03,578 --> 00:36:06,205
because you're on the run from the cops?

441
00:36:08,791 --> 00:36:12,170
I've turned my life around, Camia.

442
00:36:13,379 --> 00:36:16,299
Back in prison, I realized
that being a criminal is hard.

443
00:36:16,382 --> 00:36:17,925
You don't have a future,

444
00:36:18,009 --> 00:36:19,844
and the law will never be kind to you.

445
00:36:20,595 --> 00:36:23,097
I've turned my back on
my old life since then.

446
00:36:24,390 --> 00:36:25,433
[sighs]

447
00:36:28,769 --> 00:36:30,062
All right, Damian.

448
00:36:31,480 --> 00:36:33,649
I'll choose to believe you

449
00:36:34,275 --> 00:36:37,069
because if Dante were still alive,

450
00:36:37,153 --> 00:36:39,530
I'm sure he'd do the same thing.

451
00:36:39,614 --> 00:36:41,574
Because he cares for you.

452
00:36:44,202 --> 00:36:45,286
Thanks, Camia.

453
00:36:51,042 --> 00:36:52,126
Ah…

454
00:36:56,839 --> 00:37:00,134
Anyway, you should eat. The food is ready.

455
00:37:05,765 --> 00:37:07,183
<i>I'm sorry, Dante.</i>

456
00:37:07,850 --> 00:37:11,145
<i>Looks like I won't just be</i>
<i>reclaiming Jaguar's identity.</i>

457
00:37:11,938 --> 00:37:16,817
<i>I might have to take Camia</i>
<i>away from you too.</i>

458
00:37:19,487 --> 00:37:20,529
Eat up.

459
00:37:21,030 --> 00:37:23,449
[tense music playing]

460
00:37:26,577 --> 00:37:30,248
Here. This was your brother's favorite.

461
00:37:30,331 --> 00:37:31,832
-It's okay, I'll do it.
-Just help yourself, okay?

462
00:37:31,916 --> 00:37:35,086
Sure, thanks. Won't you join me?

463
00:37:35,169 --> 00:37:37,505
Go ahead. I'll eat later. Thanks.

464
00:37:37,588 --> 00:37:39,966
[tense music continues playing]

465
00:37:45,930 --> 00:37:48,474
[tense music swelling]

466
00:37:53,396 --> 00:37:55,064
Don't move around too much, Damian.

467
00:37:55,147 --> 00:37:56,732
It might get worse.

468
00:37:57,566 --> 00:38:01,445
Sorry for bothering you. And Lily too.

469
00:38:04,365 --> 00:38:08,577
If you went to a clinic,
even to the one in town,

470
00:38:08,661 --> 00:38:10,413
you'd heal up in no time.

471
00:38:10,871 --> 00:38:14,375
I don't need to. You're here, anyway.

472
00:38:14,458 --> 00:38:15,459
[groans]

473
00:38:15,543 --> 00:38:17,336
You can take care of me.

474
00:38:19,964 --> 00:38:20,881
Damian!

475
00:38:24,927 --> 00:38:28,055
What's the real reason you're
here in Poblacion Ardiente?

476
00:38:30,975 --> 00:38:35,396
When I got out of prison,
I set up a small business.

477
00:38:36,897 --> 00:38:38,691
I had somebody else manage it.

478
00:38:39,400 --> 00:38:41,819
But now, he doesn't want
to give turn it over back to me.

479
00:38:42,903 --> 00:38:47,491
He's here in Ardiente,
that's why I'm here too.

480
00:38:47,867 --> 00:38:49,410
It's dangerous here.

481
00:38:50,786 --> 00:38:52,204
Especially for you.

482
00:38:53,289 --> 00:38:54,582
What do you mean?

483
00:38:55,249 --> 00:38:57,501
Damian, you look exactly like Dante.

484
00:38:58,502 --> 00:39:01,547
If you aren't careful, they
might set their sights on you,

485
00:39:01,630 --> 00:39:03,424
just like what they did to Dante.

486
00:39:07,219 --> 00:39:10,389
What did the Ardientes do to Dante?

487
00:39:11,640 --> 00:39:13,934
[tense music playing]

488
00:39:20,024 --> 00:39:23,152
Dante was killed
by the most powerful family

489
00:39:23,235 --> 00:39:27,948
in Poblacion Ardiente years ago.

490
00:39:30,117 --> 00:39:31,702
Emilia Ardiente was the one behind it.

491
00:39:34,246 --> 00:39:35,164
[Emilia] <i>Jaguar.</i>

492
00:39:36,582 --> 00:39:38,417
<i>I thought you weren't coming.</i>

493
00:39:43,506 --> 00:39:45,966
[tense music playing]

494
00:39:52,640 --> 00:39:55,893
Ma'am, according to police
records in Manila,

495
00:39:55,976 --> 00:40:00,314
Damian Cruz has been
on the run since 2004.

496
00:40:01,190 --> 00:40:02,400
Here's his file.

497
00:40:07,905 --> 00:40:10,741
And we've also confirmed
that Emilia Ardiente escaped.

498
00:40:12,952 --> 00:40:15,788
I know. But how exactly?

499
00:40:16,163 --> 00:40:18,416
How isn't the question, but who?

500
00:40:19,166 --> 00:40:20,626
A few men helped her escape.

501
00:40:20,960 --> 00:40:24,755
A group of men, and a masked man.

502
00:40:25,381 --> 00:40:26,966
A masked man?

503
00:40:29,176 --> 00:40:31,679
[tense music playing]

504
00:40:45,443 --> 00:40:51,073
You don't have to go back home.
You can't trust your father.

505
00:40:52,032 --> 00:40:56,245
If you go back there, I'm sure
he'll have you arrested himself.

506
00:40:56,620 --> 00:40:59,290
I need to know the truth about my mother.

507
00:40:59,874 --> 00:41:02,585
Emilia, you don't need to feel…

508
00:41:03,711 --> 00:41:08,799
like something's missing in your life

509
00:41:08,883 --> 00:41:12,094
just because you don't know
who your real mother is.

510
00:41:16,974 --> 00:41:18,517
I'm here for you.

511
00:41:19,727 --> 00:41:21,353
I can give you the love you never had.

512
00:41:24,064 --> 00:41:25,399
-Emilia?
-Jaguar…

513
00:41:25,733 --> 00:41:30,362
I want to see your face,
the face of my protector.

514
00:41:32,740 --> 00:41:34,492
Why are you scared?

515
00:41:35,367 --> 00:41:38,204
I'll accept you no matter who you are,

516
00:41:38,287 --> 00:41:39,872
no matter what you look like.

517
00:41:46,629 --> 00:41:47,588
Jaguar?

518
00:42:00,184 --> 00:42:01,393
[reporter] <i>With the upcoming</i>
<i>national elections</i>

519
00:42:01,477 --> 00:42:02,811
<i>being held tomorrow,</i>

520
00:42:02,895 --> 00:42:06,232
<i>Poblacion Ardiente will witness the race</i>

521
00:42:06,315 --> 00:42:08,776
<i>between Congressman Julio Ardiente</i>

522
00:42:08,859 --> 00:42:11,695
<i>and his grandson, Diego Ardiente-Torillo.</i>

523
00:42:11,779 --> 00:42:13,197
<i>Who will you be voting for?</i>

524
00:42:14,698 --> 00:42:20,496
Thank you, people of Sto. Niño.
Just a reminder,

525
00:42:20,579 --> 00:42:23,707
please don't forget to vote
at the elections tomorrow.

526
00:42:24,458 --> 00:42:26,168
We shouldn't give in to the fear

527
00:42:26,252 --> 00:42:28,212
that they're trying to sow in us

528
00:42:28,295 --> 00:42:31,966
because we will make the voices

529
00:42:32,049 --> 00:42:35,594
of the people of Ardiente be heard.

530
00:42:35,678 --> 00:42:37,638
-That's right!
-Am I right?

531
00:42:37,721 --> 00:42:39,890
[cheering]

532
00:42:42,226 --> 00:42:44,937
-Diego!
-Diego!

533
00:42:45,020 --> 00:42:47,356
Let them hear the people's voice!

534
00:42:47,439 --> 00:42:49,149
To our victory!

535
00:42:50,025 --> 00:42:51,944
Hey! Hey! Hey! Wait!

536
00:42:52,027 --> 00:42:53,404
Hey! What's going on?

537
00:42:53,487 --> 00:42:55,322
-It's Sanggano!
-Hey!

538
00:42:57,783 --> 00:42:59,785
Hey! Listen up, everyone!

539
00:43:00,703 --> 00:43:02,621
To everybody on this list,

540
00:43:03,789 --> 00:43:06,458
if you don't vote for Julio Ardiente,

541
00:43:06,542 --> 00:43:09,003
then you better not show up here tomorrow.

542
00:43:09,086 --> 00:43:10,045
Is that clear?

543
00:43:10,129 --> 00:43:11,505
[overlapping dialogue]

544
00:43:11,589 --> 00:43:14,800
Hold on! What are you doing?

545
00:43:14,883 --> 00:43:17,803
Who are you to deprive us
of our human rights?

546
00:43:17,886 --> 00:43:20,139
You need to get out of our territory!

547
00:43:20,222 --> 00:43:25,144
That's right! The Ardientes' minions
should never set foot here!

548
00:43:25,227 --> 00:43:26,478
That's right!

549
00:43:26,562 --> 00:43:31,692
They're just trying to scare us
because they failed to buy

550
00:43:31,775 --> 00:43:33,986
the votes of the other town.

551
00:43:34,069 --> 00:43:35,904
But we aren't scared of you!

552
00:43:36,780 --> 00:43:38,866
-Is that so?
-Hey! Hey! Hey!

553
00:43:38,949 --> 00:43:41,619
-Let go of me!
-You should be tied up!

554
00:43:41,702 --> 00:43:43,495
Don't touch me! How dare you!

555
00:43:43,579 --> 00:43:46,081
-Hey! You bastard!
-[people clamoring]

556
00:43:46,165 --> 00:43:50,085
Come on! Come on! Is that all you've got?

557
00:43:50,169 --> 00:43:51,962
-[crowd screams]
-Hey! Hey!

558
00:43:52,921 --> 00:43:55,466
-Hey!
-[clamoring]

559
00:43:57,092 --> 00:43:58,344
[Loring screams]

560
00:44:00,262 --> 00:44:02,222
How could you even kill an old man?!

561
00:44:02,973 --> 00:44:05,351
-What do you want?!
-You keep getting in our way!

562
00:44:05,434 --> 00:44:07,436
The only reason you're still alive
after stealing from me

563
00:44:07,519 --> 00:44:09,104
is that I chose not to get back at you.

564
00:44:09,188 --> 00:44:10,022
Do you understand?

565
00:44:10,105 --> 00:44:13,817
That money was never yours,
and you're never getting it back.

566
00:44:13,901 --> 00:44:16,487
You better leave now or else!

567
00:44:16,570 --> 00:44:19,907
Is that a threat? All right,
then. You asked for it.

568
00:44:21,033 --> 00:44:23,619
-Come on. Fight me! Come at me!
-You can do it, Boss!

569
00:44:24,370 --> 00:44:25,579
[Anna] Diego! Jepoy!

570
00:44:27,498 --> 00:44:28,540
[crowd screams]

571
00:44:29,500 --> 00:44:30,584
Diego, get up!

572
00:44:35,089 --> 00:44:36,173
[man] Be careful, Diego!

573
00:44:37,257 --> 00:44:38,300
[groans]

574
00:44:38,384 --> 00:44:41,929
[clamoring]

575
00:44:47,059 --> 00:44:48,519
[man] Out of the way! Out of the way!

576
00:44:52,064 --> 00:44:55,025
If you don't want to ruin
Julio Ardiente's name,

577
00:44:55,109 --> 00:44:56,485
then you better leave right now.

578
00:44:57,111 --> 00:44:58,153
Leave!

579
00:44:58,237 --> 00:44:59,947
-[man] Leave!
-[man 2] Get out of here!

580
00:45:00,030 --> 00:45:02,157
[crowd clamoring]

581
00:45:02,241 --> 00:45:03,992
-Go away!
-Leave!

582
00:45:04,535 --> 00:45:05,619
Leave!

583
00:45:05,702 --> 00:45:07,162
Get away from here!

584
00:45:08,038 --> 00:45:09,123
Go!

585
00:45:09,957 --> 00:45:10,999
Leave!

586
00:45:13,877 --> 00:45:15,921
-Uncle Pandoy!
-I'm fine.

587
00:45:16,004 --> 00:45:17,840
Uncle, are you okay?
Nanny, did they hurt you?

588
00:45:17,923 --> 00:45:19,299
-No, I'm fine.
-Thank you.

589
00:45:19,383 --> 00:45:21,593
-Anna, are you okay?
-I'm okay.

590
00:45:21,677 --> 00:45:24,638
-Did anybody get hurt?
-No, we're fine.

591
00:45:24,721 --> 00:45:25,639
What about you?

592
00:45:25,722 --> 00:45:27,474
-I'm fine.
-Make sure those oafs are gone.

593
00:45:31,562 --> 00:45:34,398
[tense music playing]

594
00:45:47,995 --> 00:45:49,496
[Raul] <i>If I tell you who I really am,</i>

595
00:45:49,580 --> 00:45:52,124
<i>how can I be sure that you won't leave me?</i>

596
00:45:52,207 --> 00:45:53,250
<i>Jaguar…</i>

597
00:45:54,376 --> 00:45:56,336
<i>There's something you need to know.</i>

598
00:45:57,713 --> 00:46:01,091
[Camia] <i>Diego, this is the day</i>
<i>we've been waiting for.</i>

599
00:46:01,175 --> 00:46:03,427
<i>I will be the governor of this town.</i>

600
00:46:03,510 --> 00:46:05,137
<i>To the future of Ardiente!</i>

601
00:46:05,220 --> 00:46:06,513
<i>Diego!</i>

602
00:46:06,597 --> 00:46:08,640
[Julio] <i>I have a plan.</i>

603
00:46:08,724 --> 00:46:12,269
<i>And in this plan,</i>
<i>my victory will be certain.</i>

604
00:46:12,352 --> 00:46:14,104
<i>We'll just have to blow things up.</i>

605
00:46:15,564 --> 00:46:17,065
[explosions]

606
00:46:17,149 --> 00:46:18,358
[Julio] <i>You're the bomb.</i>

607
00:46:18,442 --> 00:46:20,402
[laughing wickedly]

608
00:46:20,486 --> 00:46:23,030
[theme music playing]
